== the big change that went wrong in plain sight
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-85
calls: UR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, elder, rival
cast_want: lead_crisis
lead_way: knowing
earth: you lead at a place you go: people follow you because your plans work, and this season a plan of yours failed where everyone could see
times: Authority that rests on expertise is accepted while the expert is seen to be right; one visible failure of judgement weakens it far more than private doubts (French and Raven 1959)
gap: 3-8
scene: {N} has led {place} for years on knowing best, and people go along because {Ns} plans usually work. This season {N} pushed through a big change against the doubts of {colleague}, and it has gone wrong in plain sight: the work is behind and people had to stay late to put it right. At the next gathering the doubters sit in the front row. {N} is still in charge, but nobody is sure for how long.
scene W: {N} made the call alone and it hurt everyone; the fair thing is to let the people it hurt have their say.
scene U: Somewhere in the plan is the exact point where it broke, and {N} cannot rest until it is found.
scene B: A leader who looks wrong once can be pushed aside; {N} counts who still owes {N} their place.
scene R: The worst thing now would be to look beaten; people want a leader with fire in them, not excuses.
scene G: The old way worked for years before {N} changed it, and the people who said so have not forgotten.
- W | own the mistake formally, and hand the next big decision to a vote of everyone | lead: rules | v: universalism, conformity | mark: owned up | chance: 70
- U | show exactly where the plan failed, and bring a corrected plan the next morning | lead: knowing | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 75
- B | quietly make it up to the people it cost most, so they owe you again | lead: favours | v: power | act: quietly make it up to the people it cost most, so they owe them again | chance: 65
- R | stand up, laugh at yourself, and promise a bold new start they can all share | lead: inspiring | v: stimulation, self-direction | act: stand up, laugh at themselves, and promise a bold new start they can all share | chance: 60
- G | go back to the way {place} always did it, and say so plainly | lead: custom | v: tradition, security | chance: 80
- W>U | set up a fair review, with {colleague} on it, to find what went wrong | lead: rules | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 70
- U>B | lay out the facts so the blame falls on parts others ran, and keep going | lead: knowing | v: power, achievement | mark: made an enemy | chance: 65
- B>R | call in favours to throw a gathering that lifts everyone after the bad season | lead: favours | v: hedonism, power | chance: 75
- R>G | bring everyone together and remind them what {place} means to all of them | lead: inspiring | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 80
- G>W | ask {elder} and the old hands to judge the matter, as the place always has | lead: custom | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 60
works: By the end of the year the bad season is a story people tell with a smile, and {N} is still the one they turn to.
works: {colleague}, who doubted the plan, ends up working closely with {N} on the next one.
fails: The doubters stay in the front row, and every new idea {N} brings is met with the question of last season.
fails: {rival} quietly gathers backing, and {N} hears {Ns} name spoken more carefully than it used to be.

== the warning the expert waved away
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-85
calls: WBG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community
