- B | call in what people owe you to keep {rival} from gaining ground | lead: favours | v: power | mark: made an enemy | act: call in what people owe them to keep {rival} from gaining ground | chance: 65
- R | admit it boldly, then take on the hardest fix yourself, in front of everyone | lead: inspiring | v: stimulation, achievement | mark: owned up | act: admit it boldly, then take on the hardest fix themselves, in front of everyone | chance: 60
- G | keep to the steady old ways, say little, and let time mend it | lead: custom | v: tradition, security | chance: 80
- W>B | push a rule that settles disputes by rank, so your word stays final | lead: rules | v: power, conformity | act: push a rule that settles disputes by rank, so their word stays final | chance: 70
- U>R | drop the cautious method and try the daring new one you have been itching to test | lead: knowing | v: stimulation, self-direction | act: drop the cautious method and try the daring new one they have been itching to test | chance: 65
- B>G | do quiet favours for the old hands until they count you as one of them again | lead: favours | v: benevolence, tradition | act: do quiet favours for the old hands until they count them as one of them again | chance: 75
- R>W | rally everyone behind a promise: a fair hearing for any warning, from anyone | lead: inspiring | v: universalism, stimulation | chance: 80
- G>U | ask {elder} what the warning meant in the old days, and learn from it | lead: custom | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 60
