scene W: {N} sees it plainly now: a place that runs on who can fix what for whom was never quite fair, and it was bound to wobble.
scene U: {N} wants to know which of the old favours really mattered to people, and which were just habit. The answer decides what to do.
scene B: {N} lost one lever, not all of them. Somewhere there is a new deal to strike before {rival} takes the rest.
scene R: {N} cannot believe people would leave over a few favours. {N} wants to look them in the eye and ask.
scene G: {place} was here long before {Ns} post, and its people belonged to it, not to whoever could pull strings.
