times: People follow a leader for position, expertise, rewards or admiration, and a long absence shows which of these was really holding them (French and Raven 1959)
gap: 3-8
scene: After a long winter laid up at home, {N} comes back to {place} to find {colleague} has been running things, and running them differently. Some of it works better, and some of it {N} would never have done. A few regulars say it is time {N} handed over for good; others say the place is not the same without {N}. {colleague} waits to hear what {N} will do.
scene W: {colleague} kept {place} going when it mattered, and {N} owes them a handover that is clean and fair.
scene U: {N} can see exactly what {colleague} changed, and which changes worked; the question is what the evidence says.
scene B: {N} built the ties that keep {place} going, and is not ready to see them pass to someone who did not.
scene R: Seeing {colleague} light the place up in a new way stirs something in {N}: pride, and a pang.
scene G: {N} has grown old with {place}, and wonders whether the place is ready for someone new, or {N} is.
- W | name the one who held things together as your successor, properly and in writing | hand: chosen | v: conformity, benevolence | act: name the one who held things together as their successor, properly and in writing | chance: 80
- U | weigh how the place ran with and without you, then open the post on results | hand: open | v: self-direction, universalism | act: weigh how the place ran with and without them, then open the post on results | chance: 65
- B | take the reins back: the people who owe you expect you, not a stand-in | hand: stay | v: power | act: take the reins back, since the people who owe them expect them, not a stand-in | chance: 70
- R | hand over now with a big night, passing your spark to whoever kept it lit | hand: chosen | v: stimulation, benevolence | act: hand over now with a big night, passing their spark to whoever kept it lit | chance: 75
- G | step back and let the regulars choose, the way the place has always settled such things | hand: open | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 75
- W>U | set clear, fair rules for an open contest judged on what each one has achieved | hand: open | v: universalism, achievement | chance: 60
- U>B | stay on as the one who knows how it really works, and keep the final say | hand: stay | v: power, achievement | chance: 75
- B>R | call in old favours to set up your chosen heir, then go and enjoy your freedom | hand: chosen | v: power, hedonism | act: call in old favours to set up their chosen heir, then go and enjoy their freedom | chance: 70
- R>G | rally the whole place for an open gathering, so whoever wins belongs to everyone | hand: open | v: stimulation, tradition | chance: 65
- G>W | stay on, as elders here always have, until fair rules for choosing are agreed | hand: stay | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 65
works: {colleague} and {N} come out of it on good terms, and {place} has a steady year.
works: The regulars who doubted come round, and {place} feels settled again before long.
fails: {colleague} takes it hard, and the two of them barely speak for a season.
fails: The regulars split over it, and {place} limps through a tense year.
